<title>SWITZERLAND: Baloise names price for Belgian offer.</title>
<headline>Baloise names price for Belgian offer.</headline>
<dateline>BASLE, Switzerland 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swiss insurer Baloise Holding said it was offering 12,125 Belgian francs per share to minority shareholders for the remaining stake in its Belgian unit Mercator &amp; Noordstar.</p>
<p>A Baloise spokesman named the price in answer to enquiries after earlier announcing that a public offer for the minority stake.</p>
<p>Baloise currently holds 53 percent in the Belgian insurer, created from the recently completed merger of Baloise subsidiary Mercator with Noordstar.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Newsroom, +41-1-631 7340</p>
</text>
